Well, whatever the evils of Microsoft Outlook Express, please check
your line endings. The above is definitely not easy to read.

(Netscape started this silly idea of breaking the lines when posting
and not in the editor where you could see what it would look like and
still have the advantage of a flowing paragraph. Then Microsoft
dutifully emulated this behavior. 

There is good reason to think this was done to encourage the use of
HTML. HTML has other problems for interactive (discussion) use,
however. There are problems with editing followups that includes
quoted text, for example. And (judiciously) quoting text is useful, in
particular when following sprawling threads.

One shouldn't think that because HTML is an ideal fit for the web that
it's an ideal fit for all sorts of things.)

The easiest way to avoid the problem, with the existing software, is
to write slightly shorter lines so you don't run into the dumb
auto-wrapping. Another idea is to not type Enter at all and let the
newsposter reflow. I guess that was the idea but it sure isn't
intuitive.

Note crosspost. For an extended discussion of formatting, please go to
news.software.readers, where this is crossposted.



