:I've got my hands on an old MicroVAX 3100. The model mumber is DV-31CT2-A so
:which model is it? 30?

  Likely a MicroVAX 3100 model 20.  Beware -- this system will have the 
  1.073 GB system disk maximum capacity limitation discussed over in the 
  OpenVMS Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ).  This MicroVAX system is 
  roughly equivilent to the VAXstation 3100 model 40 system, less the
  graphics capabilities of the latter...

:I'm thinking about putting NetBSD on it, but roughly how fast is it? 
:I mean if you comparare to a PC... 486?

  Performance questions of decade-old hardware?

  The way-old SPEC numbers were -- way back when the VAX-11/780 was 1 
  in the particular SPEC benchmarks -- circa 2.4.  (This would have 
  been what was later known as SPECmark89?)  For comparision, one of
  the i486 systems at 33MHz was rated at circa 8.8 SPECmark89.

  Get an old Alpha and run Linux or OpenVMS.  You'll be happier.  :-)

