If you want to run both you'll need to concentrate on a card supported by
OpenVMS, I've got a friend that is currently using a generic S3 card in one
of his.  I'm currently using the S3 card that DEC shipped.  I don't believe
Linux supports the better TGA cards, and I don't know about Linux support
for any of the others.

You can run OpenVMS without a card no problem, but Linux needs patched to
use a serial terminal, so you'd need a video card for the install at least.

