In article <36FBFC77.BBF2864F@srv.net>, Kevin Handy <kth@srv.net> writes:
:I have just got an AlphaStation 200 4/100 system (PB40A-AA)
:without any kind of graphics card in it.  Is there any place
:that I can find what cards are supported by this system, and
:how much one would cost?

  The AlphaStation 200 4/100 is very slow...

  The PowerStorm 3D30 (PBXGB-AA) is one of the more common graphics 
  controllers found in these systems.

  The PowerStorm 3D30 works with OpenVMS, Tru64 UNIX, and Windows NT.

  OpenVMS, Tru64 UNIX, and Windows NT all also support the PBXGA-AA 
  ZLXp-E1, PBXGA-BA ZLXp-E2, and PBXGA-CA ZLXp-E3 graphics controllers.

  There are a few others; a PowerStorm 4D series would likely be overkill.

  I do not know the prices for these (or other) used graphics controllers.
  Check with the various used-equipment vendors around...

:I would like to use it with OpenVMS and Linux.

  I do not know which graphics controllers Linux has drivers for.

