them.  The 10 year old Honda I drive recently had a failure in the
latch that opens the hood.  That prevented me from adding wiper fluid,
which is a major transportation impediment with the residue of Northeast
snow storms splashing onto the windshield in heavy traffic.  One latch
in 10 years is probably minor on the parts-and-labor front, but for me
it was major in the denial-of-service department.  It also took them a
few days to acquire the part, which is not of significant concern to
the repair agency but certainly is to the victim.

