"Forest Gum" <Trishgoff@hotmail.com> writes...
}Anyone can advise how to use the lexical function to suppress "," so =
}that I can
}convert the numberic string into figure for caluation.
}i.e. read from file that contain 1,234,445,233 convert to 1234445223.

Try this:

$ A = "1,234,445,233"
$ B = A -","-","-","
$ Write Sys$Output B
$ Write Sys$Output B+1

It subtracts up to 3 "," from A when making B. If A has fewer than 3, the
excess subtractions do not do anything. If A can have more, you might want
to do more than 3 (but you won't be able to do any math with the result
since DCL uses 32 bit signed integers which would never have more than 3
of them).

--- Carl



