In article <36FA15C7.5F82@alert-systems.com>, Henk Borsje <hjborsje@alert-systems.com> writes:
> One of my RZ25's is reporting frequent errors and probalby will need
> replacement.  I still use VMS 5.5 on the machine.  What is a good
> third-party disk that can serve as replacement?

5.5 ?  I'd advise you to stick to older drives, as the SCSI disk drivers
won't be all that tolerant of any strange new features in modern disks.
Either try to pick up a used RZ25 or RZ26, or go for something like an
early Seagate Hawk of about 1Gb capacity.  Likely models are ST31200N,
ST31230N, perhaps ST11200N.  Early Quantum Fireballs are not recommended.

> I know there is a maximum size of 1 GIG drives on VAXstations 3100. Is
> the limit on a 4000/60 different?

Yes, it is not really limited at all.  Except you can't go beyond 8Gb with
that version of VMS, and I wouldn't recommend going past 4Gb in this
enclosure.

> After replacing the disk (it is not the system disk), is an 'init'
> command sufficient to set up the disk?

Should be.  Resist the temptation to do any low-level formatting - most
folks seem to find this makes problems worse.

