"Brian Steele" <omigosh@caribsurf.com> writes...
}What sort of performance degradation can I expect if I backup my 7610's disk
}drives across an ethernet link to a SCSI tape drive connected to an
}Infoserver 1000, instead of to a tape drive that's connected directly to the
}7610?
} 
}Thanks,
}Brian Steele

It depends. You have not provided sufficient information to tell.

How fast is the tape drive on the system?
How fast is the tape drive on the Infoserver?
How fast is your network?
Is the network, at least the parts in question, switched or shared (i.e.
hubs/repeaters instead of switches)?
How busy is your network (just the parts that will be used for the data
transfer if it is switched)?

If the tape drive on the Infoserver is the same speed as the one in
the system (i.e. you were to move the same drive from the system to
the Infoserver) and the network is fast enough to systain data transfers
at the full speed of the drive (for example, the drive does not more
than 1MB/sec for a 10mb/s network) and is not loaded from other sources in
a way that will adversely impact the performance of the parts of the network
in question sufficiently to drop the sustainable throughput too low, then
you will get identical performance.

--- Carl



