At this point in the game, the overall cost isn't the issue (not yet). 
But, because of the limited funding in education, we don't get to
purchase new technology frequently; in fact, we are usually forced to
continue with outdated, and sometimes unsupported, technology.  So, our
first issue is whether or not OpenVMS will be alive and kicking 5-10
years down the road.  We've been on our current platform for 6 years,
and it will most likely have to make it to at least 7.

Although I haven't received approval to purchase the reports yet, I have
already found a couple that state that Compaq-Digital has already
announced that OpenVMS will no longer receive R&D funds by the end of
2001 - if this is true, then it seems logical that end of support would
follow....  

