The most common compiler internal error problem that's been reported
for C++ V6.0-010 is that the compiler core dumps on boolean literals
in conditional expressions, i.e.:

  b ? true : false;

This has been fixed in the latest V6.0 compiler (DIGITAL C++ V6.0-021).
It is also fixed in the released version of V6.1 (DIGITAL C++ V6.1-029).
