At Tue, 23 Mar 1999 16:40:39 +0100 adrian
(adrian@gmx.li) wrote:
> hi,
> maybe one of you can help:i obtained an personal decstation5k/25 ,but
> whitout monitor and keyboard.so my question is how i can use this
> thing,i ve tried to connect a terminal (suns are also switching
> automatically console) but it didnt work.
> any idee.

Maybe the clear-NVR jumper as described in "Personal DECstation 5000
Hardware Maintenance Guide" works:

o First locate the two-pin nvr connector, if you're in front of the
machine it's located left from the power connecter and marked "nvr".

o Slide a jumper over the nvr connector.

o Turn on the system power and wait for the console prompt to appear.

o When the console prompt appears, turn off the system power again.

o Remove the jumper from the nvr connector.


You can set the console and above described operation clears it, then a
properly set-up (9600, 8n1) terminal should work.

-- 
Richard

