Alan,

Yes.  You can almost always use faster cache chips (and memory) than
required, because the memory takes its timing from the motherboard,
not vice versa.  The cache chip speed is the fastest speed at which
they are rated to operate at.  They can always run slower.  

I have a stock of new 32Kx8 20 ns. cache RAM chips here at $4.50
apiece.  + exact shipping and an installation guide, to boot.

