Try use BIND graphical configuration tool (you cand find it in CDE progam
folder) Specify DNS server address and domain name, and configure the DNS
server, if your DU box should be this DNS server. The tool will ask you:  -
should inet service seek addresses in /etc/host before using DNS?
- which host name should be used - with <dot>doman_name or without it?
Also you can configure it using BIND configuration utility, (ascii-based
interface).
# setup
or
it displays menu
                           1-Configure network intefaces ...
                           2- ....
                           3- ...
                             .....
                           <last number depends on your kernel configuration
and  subsets   installed > - ...
Select the  BIND and configure that. Utility will make all the neccessary
modifications in the configuration files.
aslo try read the output of something like following:
man bind
man bind_manual_setup
or
man dns_manual_setup
or even
man network_manal_setup
(don't be offended by mistakes, please - English is not my native language)
