In article <7cjcc7$cvn$3@info.service.rug.nl>, helbig@gladia.astro.rug.nl (Phillip Helbig) writes:
:Is it true that the InfoServer is no longer supported?

  InfoServers are no longer available for purchase, but are supported.

:What is the (technical) reason why write-mounted InfoServer disks cannot 
:be written to by any machine in a cluster like a `normal' disk?

  Interlocking.  Consider what extra host software is involved -- the
  OpenVMS Cluster distributed lock manager -- in order to coordinate 
  access to another famous "block server" device, the HSC50.  Like the
  HSC50, InfoServer devices are block servers, with no concept of files 
  nor shared (write/modify) access.

  Various folks have created partitions for users, allowing multiple
  users to have access to storage in a common pool -- each user has
  exclusive write access to an InfoServer partition.  (The level of
  performance of this configuration may or may not be suitable for 
  a particular application -- it will be limited by the InfoServer 
  and the network, obviously.)

 -------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
 Hoff (Stephen) Hoffman   OpenVMS Engineering   hoffman#xdelta.zko.dec.com




