The HP 4000 comes standard with *both* a serial and parallel
interface.   If you add an "N" (network) to the model number,
you also get an ethernet port.   Unfortunately, it doesn't
speak LAT.   Emulex makes an external one (plugs into the
parallel port) that does speak LAT, but their documentation
CDROM is not usable on a VMS system.

Overall, it is an excellent printer and I recommend it highly.
I suggest that you invest the extra money and get the optional
duplexer.   That saves a lot of paper when printing the
installation guides from the CONDIST.   :-)

Right now, I have the serial port connected to my VAX and
the parallel port (through a switch) to my PC and AlphaStation.

I got it from CDW (www.cdw.com).   It was delivered the
day after I ordered it!   I don't know how they do that,
but it has happened multiple times.   One time was for
the brand new HP CapShare 910, which was not even in their
price list.

