Message-ID: <7cbioq$80a@ds2.acs.ucalgary.ca>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 454262194
References: <7c9itj$pqf@gap.cco.caltech.edu>
Organization: The University of Calgary
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec

mathog@seqaxp.bio.caltech.edu wrote:
: Can somebody please point me to performance numbers for a PWS 500au with,
: and without, the L3 cache?  

It will entirely depend on your applications. For the applications
we are running, the difference is under 10%. Some applications may
even experience performance *degradation* with L3 installed. I was
told that parallel programs doing a lot of network I/O are particularly
susceptible to this problem, and would also suspect that numerical codes 
with large working sets and non-unit-stride memory access pattern 
(read: many codes tuned for vector supercomputers) will also see
performance *decrease* with L3 cache installed. On the other hand, 
many programs will benefit quite noticeably from L3.

The only way you can be sure is to measure performance difference
on your own applications.

Regards,

/Serge.P



