:only (Friday 3/12). I have been researching for an hour now, and I can't seem
:to find a use for them under Linux, only newer Dectalk units. If anyone has a
:good use for them, please email me right away before they go in the trash!

  DECtalk DTC03 devices will work quite nicely from most any platform
  that is capable of serial ASCII and ANSI control sequences.  The 
  DECtalk DTC01 and DTC03 use serial ASCII and escape sequences -- any 
  system that can communicate with a serial printer or terminal can 
  connect and operate a DECtalk DTC03. This (obviously) includes Linux 
  systems.  

  There is the source code of a DECtalk library -- overkill for the
  sort of thing most folks need -- available on the OpenVMS Freeware:

    http://www.openvms.digital.com/freeware/

  Look in the DECtalk directory.

  There are other source examples around the 'net.

:For starters, are the cabinets standard 19" racks?

  Yes.

