  Without intending to either state the obvious or to appear rude, ten 
  year old serial printers do tend to be slow by current standards...

  LN03R Dip switches:
    
    Pack 1:   1  \
              2   |  Baud Rate (see below)
              3   |
              4  /
              5  On: 7 Data Bits            Off: 8 Data Bits
              6  On: Parity per 2-1 Checked Off: Parity Not Checked
    
       Baud Rate:    1-1    1-2    1-3    1-4    Rate
    
                     Off    Off    Off    Off    1200
                     Off    Off    Off    On     2400
                     Off    Off    On     Off    3600
                     Off    Off    On     On     4800
                     Off    On     Off    Off    7200
                     Off    On     Off    On     9600*  (max recommended)
                     Off    On     On     Off   19200
                     Off    On     On     On    38400
                     On     Off    Off    Off   57600
    
    Pack 2:   1  On: Odd/Space Parity       Off: Even/Mark Parity
              2  NOT USED
              3  NOT USED
              4  On: Use DTR for Restraint  Off: Use BUSY for Restraint
              5  On: Restraint Flow Control Off: XON/XOFF Flow Control
              6  On: Restraint Inverted     Off: Restraint Normal
    
 

 
