We have encountered a backwards compatibility issue with CDE 2.x and
the old CDE version 1.x.  Seems that the old .dt/session/home/dt.session
file has been replaced by something called dtsession.db?
Not only has the filename changed, but the contents look completely
different.  This has been seen on an HP-UX 11.00 system.

So what happens is:
  - user has a home session created under CDE 1.x (and a dt.session file)
  - user logs into a CDE 2.x system, modifies and saves a new home session.
    this writes ~/.dt/sessions/home/dtsession.db, but no dt.session.
  - login back on a CDE 1.x system and, whoops!, no dt.session file found
    so display generic, default home session.

    Very wonderful.. not!

I'm really hoping the opengroup didn't design such
an un-common, common environment and that there
is some type of backward compatibility mode, at least.

Does anyone have an online reference to the latest CDE, version 2.x?

Thanks for any insight into this problem,
-allen, winterz@clark.net





