Kent Rankin wrote:
> 
> It's running Ultrix 4.3(er, attempting to<grin>), and has three
> CDC/Seagate 9720-1230 Sabre drives on SMD.  They're running alright, but
> there are some hard errors that I need to fix in order to get the system
> up and running(need to do it fast, BTW<grin>).
> 
>   I get errors as such when running fsck's:
> 
> ra2a: hard error sn 25061
> ra2a: Force Error Modifier Set: LBN 25061
> 
>   Anyone have any ideas?

You probably should low-level format the drives at some point in
time.  (After, of course, making backups!)  How you do the
low-level format will depend greatly on who made your SMD drive
controller (it wasn't DEC!)

>   BTW, I think that these have been caused by me restarting improperly.
> When the system sticks me in a bad place, I have to send a <break> to
> the system in order to get to the boot monitor(can you tell that I am a
> Sun fellow?).  From there I send a halt, and restart.  A few times of
> doing this has messed things up a bit.  =)

This'll force a fsck, which will cause a complete reread of some
of the filesystem tables, and make low-level disk errors more likely
to show up, but it shouldn't actually create the disk errors.

>   Also, if there is any way that I can keep what OS I have, I would love
> to.  I only have a copy of Ultrix 2.0 on TK50, and want to keep the copy
> of 4.3 on here(even though it has no /usr directory).

Ummm... make a backup?  (And an install tape!)  Or if all the
hard drives are identical, you can do a "rolling low-level format",
where you copy the contents of your current boot drive to a different
drive with "dd", then format your current boot drive, and then
copy the previous contents back.

Tim.



