In article <7c7r59$bep$1@news-2.news.gte.net>, "Ken D." <ken.eatspam.42@gte.net> writes:
:Does anyone know what the difference is (if any) between a DECtalk DTC01 and
:a DTC01-A?

  Nothing in particular that I am aware of.  Beyond a selection of 
  DTC01-** variants around different telephony regulatory approvals,
  and/or differing power cords, all DTC01 DECtalk devices are
  basically the same.

:I've got two DTC01's but the only references I can find are to
:DTC01-A's.

  Single line DECtalk, table-top enclosure similar to that of the
  system unit for the VT240 and VT241 series terminals.  Capable 
  only of blind-dial when calling, no call progress detection.

  There are a very few DTC01 DECtalk devices that do not have the
  telephone connection -- this generally for the country-specific 
  telephony regulatory requirements.

