If it says it is an RZ26, it is SCSI... I've got a couple of
disks like that... RF/RZ35... I believe the whole electronics
board is replaced to make it RF-series (DSSI).  The board you
have is the one required for RZ-series (SCSI).  So I don't thinkg
you'll be able to simply 'jumper it for DSSI'...

