  Operating system and version?

:I tried to put a 4 GB SCSI drive on my MicroVax 3100/76 workstation
:and it only recognizes it as a 256 MB drive.

  I will assume this is a VAXstation 3100 model 76, as there is
  no equivilent MicroVAX model available.  (There are definite
  differences among the various "3100" series models -- care in
  system identification needed if the answers are to be correct 
  for the particular platform in question...)

:Does anyone know if there is a problem with MAX size of drive
:for these systems?

  Yes, if this disk is being used as a system disk, there is.  Please 
  see the OpenVMS Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ) for details on the 
  system disk capacity limits.  The FAQ is available via a link at:

    http://www.openvms.digital.com/

  This limit is independent of the operating system, and is specific
  to the contents of the console PROMs -- it is a console limit.

  If this is a disk other than the system disk, it would help greatly 
  to know what specific disk manufacturer and model is involved, and 
  what (if anything) gets logged in the error log.

:Please email me the answer.

  Ask here, get an answer here.

