Not hardly.  Here's the fileserver for my small business:

	FIC VA-503+ motherboard			$700
	AMD K6-350				$150
	256MB 100MHz ECC SDRAM			$400
	Adaptec 3940UW	(2 channel SCSI)	$350
	3X IBM UltraStar 9GB 7200RPM disks	$1140
	Nice case, with cooling for disks	$200
	2X Intel Etherexpress 100 network cards	$120

	TOTAL					$3060

You can get a comparable machine, pre-assembled, from a vendor like Compaq
or Dell for perhaps $1000 more -- and it's basically equivalent to a Sun
UE2000 or a low-end AlphaServer, either of which cost three to ten times
as much in a similar configuration.  If you need more I/O oomph, you can
add a SCSI-SCSI RAID controller like a CMD 5440 for about $3000 and add
however many disks you find appropriate.

The price/performance of well-chosen PC hardware is basically impossible
to beat.

