If it is really latin (1) ...

That would be the plural of a (feminine) "Pentia", as
Pentii would be for (masculine) "Pentius".

However, since Pentium is obviously neuter, the Plural
must be "Pentia". But who would want to have more than
one Pentium? (2)

Now don't ask me for the plural of "Alpha" which is
definitely greek - and yes, I would like to have more
than one of them.

(1) It seems to be a mixture of greek and latin. The "fifth"
in latin is quintus (quinta, quintum), "Pent..." comes
from Greek. But the the ending "-um" is latin. I think
a greek ending should be "-on" or "-ion" (neuter).

(2) Perhaps to run FreeVMS on them? But that's not yet
an OS, just a project.



