Pat,

You probably won't be able to install the 80MHz AMD 486 and run it at
full speed.  Back in the old days of 486s, DEC was a true Intel OEM,
using only Intel CPUs, and contracting Intel to build a lot of the
motherboards inside the 486s.  

What this means is that the CPUs are 5v only, not 3.3v like many AMD
486 chips.  And the external bus clock speed is limited to 33MHz, not
the 40MHz supported by many AMD chips.

Your best bet for a speed boost is the Intel 100Mhz 5v 80486-DX4
OverDrive.  The Evergreen kit based on the AMD 133Mhz Am5x86-P75 has
an outside chance of working correctly.

You can download the service maintenance manual for the DEC LPx.

http://ie.digital.com/channel/documentation/pcdoc/declpx.htm

Not sure of the differences between LPx and LPx+.

Whatever documentation DEC has about its desktops can be found at:

http://ie.digital.com/channel/documentation/pcdoc/desktop.htm

... Ben Myers

