In article <36DC727B.FB066A2E@worldnet.att.net>, WartHog <Thomas.John@worldnet.att.net> writes:


  Please pick a relevent subject for your question -- you want to attract
  the attention of somebody that knows and can answer your question.
  Most anything could be asked under "A little help please." -- these
  generic subject lines can and often do get ignored.


:I have aquired 2 2GB Digital RZ28-E, REV E02 scsi disk drives.  I need
:the scsi addressing scheme so I can change the SCSI address with the
:jumpers.

  If this matches the other RZ28 drives, there are a clump of three 
  jumpers on the module, near the SCSI connector.  These jumpers should	
  not be altered without explicit instructions.

  To set spinup or the unit number, look at the other end of the module.
  There are a clump of ten jumpers over there, the three closest to the 
  corner of the module are the SCSI ID jumpers.  The seventh from the 
  corner is the spin-up jumper.  (In general, using RZSPINUP or similar 
  is the prefered method of setting spinup, however.)


