Julian Corallo wrote:
> 
> Yet again, still on the steep bit of the learning curve with regard to
> vax...! :-)
> 
> Sorry if this is repeat, easy question!
> 
> Every so often, I see a web-page or posting, that says 'oh, you can turn
> your vaxstation into a microvax just by flicking a switch'
> 
> Whats all that about?
> 
> What do I get thats different when its a microvax as opposed to a
> vaxstation. What about the license requirements for the base vms?


Some (not all) VAXstations can be changed into MicroVAXen.  How this is
done is model specific.  The result may be either a MicroVAX or a
VAXserver.

For example:

Removing the graphics board from a VAXstation II turns it into a
MicroVAX II.

The MicroVAX 2000 / VAXstation 2000 setting is determined by a jumper on
the motherboard.

Removing the keyboard from a VAXstation 3100 turns it into a VAXserver
3100.

Even if you remove the graphics board and keyboard, a VAXstation 4000-60
is still a VAXstation 4000-60.

As far as the license unit required, the MicroVAX, VAXserver, and
VAXstation all have different license requirements.  Generally, the
VAXserver and VAXstation licenses are less expensive.

