From what I understand of the specification documents,

unsigned long prectime(void)
{
  unsigned long pook,pook2;
  __asm__ __volatile__("rpcc %0" : "=r" (pook));
  pook2 = pook>>32;
  pook -= pook2<<32;
  pook2 += pook;
  return(pook2);
}

should give me something similar to the results of RDTSC on an x86.

Under DU4 on the big Alpha box here, it doesn't; it gives me a result on
the order of 10^6, incrementing by about 10^5 per second - which is four
orders of magnitude less accuracy than I expected and needed for some
calculations about speeds of L1 and L2 cache.

What am I doing wrong?

Tom




