Adam,
     While it is interesting how your company operates it would be easier to
answer your questions if we knew what brand and version of software you are
working with.  You do give some useful information 1) its OpenVMS you are
working with and 2) you have Digital TCP/IP Services for OpenVMS (UCX) for
your IP transport.

So, assuming you have UCX version 4.x here are some reference commands:

$ UCX
UCX> SHOW VERSION
    <this will give useful information to post>

UCX> HELP
    <the "man" pages>

UCX> SET ROUTE /GATEWAY=<gateway-address> /DEFAULT

Actually, I prefer to use the menu interface for modifying most of the UCX
characteristics...

$ SET DEFAULT SYS$MANAGER
$ @UCX$CONFIG

        ...Mike
