kncharyulu@my-dejanews.com wrote in message
<7bqqg4$eut$1@nnrp1.dejanews.com>...
>We want to connect SCSI Drives on VAX3400.
>Does anybode deal with SCSI Controllers on VAX3400?
>
Yes, I've done several.  The traditional DEC way was to get a DSSI to
SCSI adapter (don't remember the part number), but the best way,
providing you have a free Q-BUS slot, is to get a CMS CQD-220 (221 was
the version for 3000s???) SCSI controller.  This board did everything,
disk and tape, and you could even dual port the SCSI bus across 2
machines if you had a cluster, far cheaper than an HSC.  I ran a pair of
them on a 3400 and a 4200 for several years in a cluster, with all kinds
of drives, and it worked with every SCSI drive I ever put on it,
Seagate, DEC, Micropolis, even the cheap Quantum drives which
historically never worked right on DEC SCSI controllers.
         Jack Peacock




