Hi,

> Does anyone know what kind of memory the DECpc AXP 150 uses?  I've got some
> standard 72 pin RAM lying around, and I'd like to know if I'll blow the
> motherboard if I put it in.
I don't think you'll blow the board, but they possibly won't work. The
AXP 150 needs standard 72pin RAMs /with true parity/ (AKA ECC RAM). You
don't have a chance without parity. I'm not sure if it has to be 
FastPage, but I suspect it - EDO is too new for the AXP 150. I'm not
sure if there even is such a thing as EDO w/Parity :) You always need
4 identical modules per bank (and remember the banks are "interlaced"
on the board, AB ABAB AB from one end to the other, so first put 4
Modules in A, then if you want to, another 4 into B. A and B don't have to
be the same modules, but all A and all B have to be identical) The
maximum of memory in the AXP 150 is 256 MB in 8 32 MB SIMMs.

