> I am new to this group and it may show: What exactly is "OpenVMS Hobbyst V2.0"

See http://www.montagar.com/hobbyist/index.html for the announcementand details.
Basically, it's a set of free OpenVMS and associated layered
product licenses for noncommercial use by DECUS members. New to version 2 is
Alpha support and includes all versions of OpenVMS through v7.2.

> ...Is there much going on with VMS shareware? I would consider doing
> shareware projects, if I get a VMS system, for the hell of it.

That would be great. One can hope that with more free compiler licenses outthere,
the VMS freeware scene will be more active. ("Shareware" usually
refers to development for a small profit, which I believe isn't permitted
under the Hobbyist license...)

