I picked up a palletload of computer stuff for parts today, and in
the pallet were two DEC VAXstation 3100 boxes and two MicroVAX 3100
boxes, plus two mono monitors.  No keyboards, but I do have one 
keyboard from a DECstation 2100 at home.  Among the four boxes
were a grand total of 4 RZ23 drives (oh, well).

Questions:

1.  What software of a unixy flavor will run on these machines?

2.  Granted the RZ23's are tiny, but it looks like the MicroVAX
    can hold 5 or 6 drives internally on the doubledecker trays,
    so what drives or tapes or such would be compatible with
    them for possible unix use?

3.  Will the mono monitors work OK on any of them?

4.  Will the DECstation 2100 keyboard or the later PC layout keyboard
    work OK on any of them?

5.  IF you were mixing and combining parts among them to make the
    best possible machine, and adding an RZ26L (from the home spare
    parts), to hopefully maximize a machine for reasonable use,
    what might be the best way to assemble all the odd parts.

6.  The interface seemed to be a plain centronics style connector
    scsi interface.  Will normal non-DEC scsi things such as an
    outboard Sun shoebox or tape drive work OK on the DEC hardware?

7.  Any other recommendations into making one a reasonable home unix
    box?

Thanks

Bob Keys

    





