:    what might be the best way to assemble all the odd parts.

  That depends on the specific model system -- there are a variety 
  of VAXstation 3100 and MicroVAX 3100 systems.  Some are very fast.
  Some are not.

:6.  The interface seemed to be a plain centronics style connector
:    scsi interface.  Will normal non-DEC scsi things such as an
:    outboard Sun shoebox or tape drive work OK on the DEC hardware?

  SCSI is called "scuzzy" for a reason -- it can be pretty scuzzy,
  and getting it to work can get interesting.  If you have to ask 
  about SCSI compatibility, you might want to use DIGITAL peripherals.
  (Peripherals tested with the systems will be the easiest approach.)
  If you want to perform your own SCSI integration and testing, then 
  you should be prepared for anything from a trivial project (once in 
  a while, you get lucky :-) to a large and complex effort involving 
  changes to drivers, firmware, and various other components. 

:7.  Any other recommendations into making one a reasonable home unix
:    box?

  UNIX?

 -------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
