>
>What do I get thats different when its a microvax as opposed to a
>vaxstation. What about the license requirements for the base vms?

You don't gain any performance or such. The main reason to turn a VAXstation
into a MicroVAX is the fact that you may run the station without one of these
strange huge graphics monitors. In fact, there are still hardware differences
between a real MicroVAX and a "reconfigured" station. 

In addition the "reconfigured" station requires now a different VMS license
(one for a MicroVAX of course). You may prevent this if you connect an
LK-keyboard to the station during startup.

