Daniel Steinmetz wrote:
> Does anyone have routines that manipulate dates and would not mind
> sharing them ? I'm interested in subtracting a certain number of days
> from todays date (format YYYYMMDD ) and getting the result in a similar
> format.

One solution is to use the C RTL like:

      integer*4 t2
      structure /tm/
        integer*4 tm_sec,tm_min,tm_hour,tm_mday,tm_mon,tm_year,
     +            tm_wday,tm_yday,tm_isdst
      endstructure
      record /tm/t
      integer*4 decc$mktime,decc$localtime
      t.tm_year=99
      t.tm_mon=2
      t.tm_mday=1
      t.tm_hour=0
      t.tm_min=0
      t.tm_sec=0
      t2 = decc$mktime(t)
      t2 = t2 - 67*(24*60*60)
      call lib$movc3(9*4,%val(decc$localtime(t2)),t)
      write(*,*) t.tm_year,t.tm_mon,t.tm_mday
      end

which surprisngly works fine on VMS Alpha 6.2 !

Arne



