Daniel,  As it turns out, back in 1972, eight years before the PC,
             a group of scientists published a set of date routines in the
             Association for Computing Machinery publication, CACM
            (Communications of the ACM). These allow date "arithmetic"
            and are not affected by Y2K or any other dates in past and 
            future centuries. They were then, and are still, reportedly the
            shortest correct date routines published in a refereed journal.

            These subprograms  are available with a sample driver (main)
            program and proper citations in the comments at:
   
            http://ftp.cac.psu.edu/pub/ger/fortran/hdk/datesub.for


