qed@pobox.com (Paul Hsieh) writes:

> While I have no beef with the Alpha design, the team or Compaq, EV7 is 
> just a "two cores on a chip" EV6 knock off if I am not mistaken.

Well, I would suggest that you take a look at the presentation from uP
Forum.  From the presentation, EV7 consists of:

21264 Core with enhancements
Integrated L2 Cache
Integrated Memory Controller(Rambus)
Integrated Interprocessor Network interface


Just looking at the memory controller, how simple do you think that a
rambus memory controller with 6GB/s read/write bandwidth and 100s of
open pages is.  Add on the fact that it supports a directory based
cache coherence.  

EV7 is a both a major architectural and circuit level design.  Which
should be ahead of just about anything else out there.  

BTW, the presentation is at http://www.digital.com/alphaoem/microprocessorforum.htm

